# Client data must NEVER enter this repo
*.secrets.env
.secrets.env
engagements/
evidence/
**/authorization/

# Client and target data — see CLAUDE.md hard rule 3
#
# These three globs exist to catch a stray per-engagement artifact (recon inventory, pre-audit
# notes, a verification writeup) if one is ever created inside this repo by mistake — engagements
# live in ~/engagements/, never here. Unanchored, `*-verification.md` also matched
# docs/specs/redgold/08-findings-and-verification.md — a real spec file, not client data — and
# because the shell's grep respects .gitignore, that file went invisible to working-tree searches.
# That is how a client name once survived into a commit undetected, caught only by a git-history
# check. The negations below keep the catch-all broad everywhere else while explicitly exempting
# the spec directory. Do not "simplify" this back to the three bare globs.
*-inventory.md
*-pre-audit.md
*-verification.md
!docs/specs/**/*-inventory.md
!docs/specs/**/*-pre-audit.md
!docs/specs/**/*-verification.md

# Build noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
